<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43881" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔζωνος</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰζ</span>-, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζώνη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-girdled</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (only in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> and <u>h.Cer.</u>), as epith. of women, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.429
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				255
			</span></i>,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> later, of
			men, <i>girt up for exercise, active</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆκος δ᾽ ὁδοῦ εὐζώνῳ ἀνδρὶ πέντε
					ἡμέραι ἀναισιμοῦνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.72
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριήκοντα ἡμερέων εὐζώνῳ
			ὁδός</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				104
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.97
			</span></i>; of light troops, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				5.4.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.35.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Demetr.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπλῖται</span> without their
			heavy shields, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				7.3.46
			</span></i>: generally, <i>well-equipped</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jo.</u>
				4.13
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. τῇ κεφαλῇ πυκτεύειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					2.19
				</span></i>
			; later, of ships, <i><span class="en">
				Max.Tyr.
				1.3
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νως</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.55
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of a garment,
				<i>well-girded</i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				342
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> metaph.,
				<i>unencumbered</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πενία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pel.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. καὶ ἐλεύθερος βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					56.6
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> in Lit. Crit.,
				<i>work-a-day, unpretending</i>; in depreciatory sense,
				<i>cheap</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὔ. καὶ οἷον εὐτελὲς εἶδος τοῦ
					λόγου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermog.
					<u>Id.</u>
					2.10
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὔ. χωρὶς εὐτελείας</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.11
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκπίπτειν τὸν λόγον εἰς τὸ
				-ότερον</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				1.5
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
